classDiagram
    class Owner {
        +str name
        +list~Pet~ pets
        +str preferred_pet_id
        +add_pet(pet) None
        +get_all_tasks() list
    }
    class Pet {
        +str id
        +str name
        +str species
        +list~Task~ tasks
        +add_task(task) None
        +update_task(task_id, changes) Task
        +mark_task_complete(task_id, today) Task
    }
    class Task {
        +str id
        +str description
        +str time
        +date due_date
        +int duration_minutes
        +str priority
        +str frequency
        +bool completed
        +datetime start
        +datetime end
        +mark_complete(today) Task
    }
    class Scheduler {
        +Owner owner
        +filter_tasks(pet_id, completed, day) list
        +sort_by_time(filters) list
        +sort_by_priority(filters) list
        +overlaps(first, second) bool
        +detect_conflicts(day) list
        +build_plan(day, available_minutes) tuple
    }
    Owner "1" o-- "0..*" Pet : cares for
    Pet "1" *-- "0..*" Task : tracks occurrences
    Scheduler --> Owner : retrieves current tasks
    Scheduler ..> Task : compares times and priorities
    note for Task "start and end are computed properties. mark_complete returns the next Task or None."
    note for Pet "mark_task_complete attaches a returned occurrence, or returns None."
